 "difference_from_codimension_one": {
  "codimension_one_chart": "x |-> graphRetract iota x + u x * e, still valued in V, because the normal direction is a line inside V and u x is a scalar",
  "codimension_m_fact": "u x lies in W, which is NOT inside V, so no copy of W inside V and no identification of the normal factor K with W may be assumed",
  "fix": "the chart maps into the PRODUCT H x W, Phi x = (iota-transpose x, u x); the repository's exists_contDiffOn_localInverse is already stated between two different spaces",
  "inverse_of_the_derivative": "written down explicitly as (y,w) |-> iota y + kappa (Q-inverse w), not obtained from a dimension count"
 },
 "hypotheses": "for the general form: an orthogonal splitting, L composed with iota is zero, and L composed with kappa is bijective. For the regular-point form: only coareaJacobian (fderiv u x0) is nonzero. NO finiteness, boundedness, integrability, regular-value or SFinite hypothesis, and NO regularity outside O.",
 "interfaces_with_proved_results": {
  "slice_eq_image_vectorGraphMap": "N intersected with the level set {u = t} is EXACTLY the graph of y |-> psi (y,t) over the parameter slice",
  "hausdorffNormalized_slice_of_levelGraphFamily": "hence the proved B2 area formula computes that fibre's normalized (n-m)-dimensional measure as a Lebesgue integral of the graph area density; WEIGHT ONE ONLY, the weighted version is not proved",
  "normDet_fderiv_mul_coareaJacobian_of_levelGraphFamily": "the family satisfies verbatim the hypotheses of last round's fibre Jacobian identity, so the two densities match on the whole chart"
 },
 "scalar_consistency": {
  "lineIsometry": "the line spanned by a unit vector as a linear isometry from R",
  "graphProj_lineIsometry": "its parameter retraction is the inner product with e",
  "isVectorGraphSplitting_of_isGraphSplitting": "the scalar IsGraphSplitting IS a vector splitting with one-dimensional normal factor",
  "codimension_one_levelGraphFamily": "from the scalar hypotheses IsGraphSplitting and gradient u x0 = c * e with c nonzero, the chart produces u (iota y + psi (y,t) * e) = t, which is exactly the hlevel shape consumed by the proved Analysis.setLIntegral_coarea_graph_family"
 },
 "is_not": [
  "no coarea formula of any codimension is proved",
  "the codimension-m regular case is NOT completed",
  "no fibrewise m-dimensional change of variables (the ambient side)",
  "no WEIGHTED codimension-m area formula (the fibre side); the analogue of setLIntegral_image_graphMap",
  "no local-to-global patching and no codimension-m weighted slice measurability",
  "nothing about the critical set, sharp finite-regularity Sard, the two Cheeger comparisons or the five Energy holes"
 ],
 "remaining_work_for_the_regular_case": [
  "ambient side: m-dimensional change of variables on the image of t |-> psi (y,t) for fixed y, on the measurePreserving_split backbone proved last round",
  "fibre side: the weighted codimension-m graph area formula, the analogue of setLIntegral_image_graphMap",
  "match the two densities with normDet_fderiv_mul_coareaJacobian_of_levelGraphFamily and assemble by Tonelli into a local coarea equality (scalar analogue setLIntegral_coarea_graph_family)",
  "countable cover and disjoint patching, plus codimension-m weighted slice measurability (scalar analogue OpenSliceMeasurable.lean)"
 ],
